From 8709b7563ca1d51aad052397c483584236b71d04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cyhhao <5381613+cyhhao@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:51:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(claude): carry retry headers on upstream error responses

Claude upstream errors dropped Retry-After, Retry-After-Ms and the
Anthropic-Ratelimit-Unified-* headers after using them for cooldowns,
so passthrough-headers never forwarded them on 429/529 responses.
Keep that allow-listed subset on the error. executionErrorMessage, the
only producer of ErrorMessage.Addon, finds header carriers through
execution wrappers with errors.As, filters them like success headers,
and puts CPA's own Retry-After (a Home round delay or a local
cooldown) in place of the upstream's Retry-After and Retry-After-Ms.

Upstream: router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI#6700 at 860a2f442.
